## Description of issue / requirement to address

We've had various orientation issues in the past when travelling down the Matryoshka of solid geometries. (See e.g. #428 , #462)

We have mentioned a solution for this too, although it has never been trialled.

> Yeah... I think at this rate we should do the simplest thing that does not involve modifying the Matryoshka reverse engineering we've presently got set up and which is fairly fragile. It's given us so many headaches. Perhaps when Ivan returns we can discuss just wrapping the underlying Solid/Shell/Face/Wires from the resulting FreeCAD ops with the Bluemira equivalents, rather than explicitly handling modification/re-creation of these every time a modification to the shape is made. We'd probably lose some functionality, but perhaps we need to take a harder look at this based on the actual functionality that we will end up using, vs. what we can afford to maintain at this stage. We can, after all, always apply labels to things after they have been created, and if we subsequently modify them and still want labels... then just re-label :/

_Originally posted by @CoronelBuendia in https://github.com/Fusion-Power-Plant-Framework/bluemira/issues/462#issuecomment-979473054_

I guess it was only a matter of time before this reared its ugly head again. Right now, I'm doing a circular pattern of a relatively complicated piece of geometry (which is perfectly valid `solid.is_valid() -> True` and `solid._shape.check() -> True`).
![image](https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/26097289/161256940-98e2bfc4-4767-477e-a08c-ad8e47188b50.png)

